    "sourceComparison": "Independent source inventory established the lower-left circle's right intersection four cells from O and the annulus intersections four and six cells from O. These given numerals identify those intersections. The current native preview prints the values below adjacent integer grid lines with no tick or leader tying them back to the circle intersection.",
    "whyBlocked": "Exercise 136 requires reading the regions from the figure. Hidden correct spec anchors and passing displacement assertions do not correct visible numbers centered under different grid lines. The annulus panel also explicitly marks one unit per cell, so its visible 4 at three cells and 6 at seven cells contradict that readable scale.",
    "affectedSurface": "Current generated SVG and both hash-bound raster captures use these label offsets. The 640px image was not visually opened after the defect was found.",
    "repairRequirement": "The author must align the given numeric labels with the actual circle-axis intersections, or use unambiguous ticks or leaders without adding answer-bearing annotations. This reviewer made no author changes and did not request or perform a repair."
